Package: cortisol.nmea
Title: Nonlinear Mixed-Effects Modeling and Simulation of Diurnal Cortisol Curves
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yuntian", "Meng", email = "yuntian7103@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Yu", "Gu", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Xing", "Qiu", role = c("aut", "ths", "cph"))
  )
Description: Fits an asymmetric scaled-logistic nonlinear mixed-effects model
    (NMEA) to sparse, irregularly sampled diurnal cortisol data, with an
    optional outlier-removal and subject-screening workflow whose steps and
    tuning parameters can be configured or switched off. Also provides a
    simulation framework that generates realistic synthetic cortisol cohorts
    from aggregate pregnancy-trimester summaries (no participant-level data are
    shipped), adds configurable contamination, compares the NMEA workflow with
    an uncleaned fit and a generalized additive mixed model, and reports curve
    recovery, outlier detection, and subject retention.
